export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/Save Pipeline\" />\n\n# Save Pipeline — Session Persistence\n\n> *All three columns persist atomically as one session package in PostgreSQL.*\n\n**Status: ✅ Phase 1 & 2 complete — compiled_output persists, conversations are API-first, localStorage purged**\n\n**Last updated: 2026-07-15 — localStorage conversation hack removed, Sentry monitoring wired**\n\n---\n\n## Current State (2026-07-15)\n\n| Column | Persists? | Detail |\n|--------|----------|--------|\n| Left column (`left_column_content`) | ✅ | Saves to `prompt_sessions` table |\n| Compiled output (`compiled_output`) | ✅ | Synced via `PromptWorkspace` state → `handleSavePrompt` |\n| Conversation messages | ✅ | API-first via `POST /api/conversations/{id}/messages` |\n| Conversation linkage | ✅ | `conversationId` persisted on `prompt_sessions` via `UpdatePromptSessionRequest` |\n| Error visibility | ✅ | All API failures → `Sentry.captureException` + `logger` → DebugPanel |\n\n---\n\n## What Changed (2026-07-15)\n\n### Conversation persistence — localStorage hacked removed\n\n`conversationStorage.addMessage()` previously used localStorage as primary storage with API as best-effort sync. Messages were lost on refresh. The entire conversation layer has been rewritten:\n\n| Method | Before | After |\n|--------|--------|-------|\n| `addMessage` | localStorage → API queue | Direct `POST /api/conversations/{id}/messages` |\n| `createConversation` | localStorage fallback with `crypto.randomUUID()` | Direct `POST /api/conversations` |\n| `saveConversation` | localStorage sync + offline queue | Direct `PUT /api/conversations/{id}` |\n| `deleteConversation` | localStorage delete + API | Direct `DELETE /api/conversations/{id}` |\n| `getConversation` | localStorage fallback | Direct `GET /api/conversations/{id}` |\n| `getAllConversations` | localStorage cache + API | Direct `GET /api/conversations` |\n\n### Conversation → session linkage\n\n- `UpdatePromptSessionRequest` (backend) now accepts `conversation_id`\n- `prompt_sessions_api.update_session()` writes `conversation_id` to PostgreSQL\n- `handleConversationChange` in `WritingAreaIndex` persists the link on every new conversation\n- `InteractiveChatInterface` receives `sessionId` prop for scoped loading\n\n### Error suppression removed\n\n- `error-suppression.ts` — deleted (was globally overriding `console.error`/`console.warn`)\n- `systemDiagnostics.ts` — console overrides removed\n- All `.catch(() => {})` replaced with `console.error` or `Sentry.captureException`\n- Every conversation operation reports to Sentry with context tags\n\n### Database schema improvements\n\n| Migration | Purpose |\n|-----------|---------|\n| `prompt_sessions.project_id` FK → `projects(id)` | Direct project scoping without joining through conversations |\n| `idx_prompt_sessions_category` | Indexed category filtering |\n| Duplicate `conversation_messages` indexes dropped | Cleaned `idx_messages_conv_created`, `idx_messages_conversation` |\n| UI tab tags inserted | `general`, `trace`, `tools`, `variables` in `tag_definitions` |\n\n### BrowserRouter replaces HashRouter\n\nClean URLs — `http://localhost:5173/prompts/{uuid}` — no `#/` hash hack.\n\n---\n\n## Remaining Work\n\n### Phase 3: Atomic session package (not started)\n\n- One API call saves all three columns together in a single transaction\n- Fix `message_count` to be computed from actual rows (`SELECT COUNT(*)`), not tracked separately\n- If any column fails to save, roll back all three — no partial saves\n\n---\n\n## Target Architecture\n\n```\nSave Template click\n  │\n  ├─► collectPromptSectionsFromUI()     ← reads DOM textareas\n  ├─► getCompiledOutput()               ← reads PromptWorkspace state\n  │\n  └─► POST /api/sessions/{id}/save      ← SINGLE atomic call\n        │\n        ├─► BEGIN TRANSACTION\n        ├─► UPDATE prompt_sessions SET left_column_content, compiled_output\n        ├─► UPDATE conversation SET message_count = (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM messages)\n        ├─► INSERT INTO prompt_versions (snapshot)\n        ├─► COMMIT\n        └─► On failure: ROLLBACK all\n```\n\n---\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `frontend/src/pages/WritingAreaIndex.tsx` | `handleSavePrompt`, `handleConversationChange`, exit notification gate |\n| `frontend/src/components/PromptWorkspace.tsx` | `compiledOutput` state, RUN handler, Milvus auto-save |\n| `frontend/src/services/conversationStorage.ts` | API-first conversation CRUD, Sentry-monitored |\n| `frontend/src/components/InteractiveChatInterface.tsx` | Chat UI, session-scoped conversation loading |\n| `backend/main.py` | API routes, `UpdatePromptSessionRequest` with `conversation_id` |\n| `backend/prompt_sessions_api.py` | Session CRUD, version management, UUID validation |\n| `frontend/src/lib/sentry.ts` | Production error monitoring |\n| `frontend/src/lib/logger.ts` | Centralized logging → DebugPanel + Sentry breadcrumbs |\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n- [ ] Click Save Template → compiled_output appears in database\n- [ ] Send message in chat → message row exists in database on refresh\n- [ ] message_count equals actual message count\n- [ ] All three columns save in one transaction\n- [ ] Failed save rolls back all columns\n"